s-fine-0021"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1315feb12780af5fa80a83d4df7a01c4cfc2c075bf0ba7ca8927255faaef9f83","title":"Does partial moduli stabilization remove every infinite-distance direction, or can the remaining flat Kähler sector still support arbitrarily large scalar excursions? The paper asks this within LVS, using the internal Kähler cone and the induced kinetic metric.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0027"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:1346637c74e520e5d2cf965d89575d05855a8acc8229050ac525ef915369288f","title":"Can an axion traverse a large canonical distance in a string-derived cosmological effective theory while heavy fields remain stabilized and all retained masses remain below the ultraviolet cutoff?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:134d4e1478bede164105461ea180e7a41159e2f787b5e3275352dff2e6dc6bee","title":"Can a planar one-loop field-theory calculation reproduce the supergravity prediction for chiral-primary one-point functions in the flux-stabilized, completely non-supersymmetric D3-D7 AdS/dCFT setup?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:135546c87cabb9be83e350dceb0fa49577c39b12cc73e9bcbf0db35537a9fad4","title":"Can a landscape account for a very small cosmological constant without calculating each vacuum energy to the observed precision?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0038"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:13e2b7935927f018ba049a3bf0464f3e0cbaac9f97924169e07217318918aa2f","title":"How much energy can escape to infinity in a collisional Penrose process involving massive spinning particles near a near-extremal Kerr-Newman black hole, and how does the reported maximum depend on particle spin?","connectionCount":1,"de